with the situation we have all
been thinking about?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.530
Isn't it all the more important
to give it serious thought

00:11:57.530 --> 00:12:00.550
because we have come
face to face with it?

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:04.300
What you did is only a
matter of outcome.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:07.040
What's more important is the intention
behind that outcome.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.510
When one dedicates one's
life toward a goal,

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:12.910
then that person will know what
path they must follow in life.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.310
Those are Mr. Nishida's words.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:14.410
You've read them yourself?
Those are Mr. Nishida's words.

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:15.900
You've read them yourself?

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.440
I think all of us are seeking
desperately for that path.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:25.960
Major Takayama... Captain Kitazawa...

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:29.290
I'm sure Captain Ataka and
Captain Kaburagi are too.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:33.060
So, what do we do?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.530
Well...

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:38.530
You want to use a TA.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:42.100
There's no question this
constitutes illegal action.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.980
But, Captain Gowa,

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.840
that girl is on the verge of slipping
from this world, right?

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.150
America...

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:55.490
They're intent on controlling hearts
and minds through force.

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:59.620
You know firsthand what a terrible
price people have had to pay.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.820
You were manipulated by a company
following that same flawed logic.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:08.030
I can only imagine what you thought
while you were made to endure that.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:11.660
But I think I understand how you're
compelled to protect that girl,

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.860
even if it means breaking laws.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:19.600
That's right. These are my
personal feelings.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:24.080
But if I betray myself now, deny these
feelings I feel right now,

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:28.940
I fear I'll have to keep betraying
myself for the rest of my life.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.450
Okay! Let's do it.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:37.190
This is my cute little baby brother's
request, after all.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:41.870
Having said that, I don't think it's
a good idea to go barging in.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.770
Don't worry about it.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:47.540
We are going to let ourselves in by
claiming we're after a criminal.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.170
I don't get it.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.580
Just listen to yourself!

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:53.680
We'd never shelter a man who tried to
assassinate your Prime Minister!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.110
There was a tip to the Department
of Public Safety and Security.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.780
Formal orders have been issued for
a peacekeeping security force

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.920
to be dispatched to
apprehend the suspect.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.220
Made Little Murai do what?

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.890
Well, I was confident that she
would have no problems

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:06.980
hacking into the SSDF's
chain of command.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:12.490
Jeez, I can't believe she's making me
do something as risky as this.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:15.500
If the Colonel ever found out...

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.940
We're merely using to our
advantage an organization

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.910
that was established two hours ago

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.270
and a law that just recently
went into effect.

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:26.310
It will be easy to come up with
plausible excuses later.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:28.710
Worse come to worse, a
bunch of higher-ups

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:30.850
will be replaced by another
lot of higher-ups.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.550
Yushiro!

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.520
This is not going to be like what
we faced in Belgistan.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:36.720
I know.

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:41.630
There's been a change in plans?

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:42.830
I'm sorry about this,

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.900
but we've cancelled our flight
back to the United States.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:49.430
Instead, I'd like you to ready
a CH-53 for flight.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:53.470
That's no problem, but what happened?

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.570
I believe a top secret weapon that
was being developed covertly

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:59.770
was delivered to this base today
by a Navy transport aircraft.

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:03.610
No, there's no need for alarm, Sir.

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:06.520
Symbol's R&D team was working
along side the DOD

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:09.950
on the development of that prototype.

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.120
I see.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.390
Official orders from the Pentagon
should be arriving shortly,

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:17.930
but we would like to have you ferry
that prototype and ourselves

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:22.370
to Symbol Japan's main
investigation headquarters.

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:25.030
Very good, Sir. I'll have my people
get to work right away.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.140
The Japanese Department of Public
Safety and Security just requested

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.370
that we hand over the suspect in
the shooting the Prime Minister

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.640
whom they believe we are sheltering.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:36.110
What?! We have no one like that here!
Are they out of their minds?

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:38.950
I told them it must be a mistake,
but they won't listen to me,

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.750
saying they're following official orders
handed down from above.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.660
They even threatened to dispatch a
peacekeeping security force

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:47.530
against the base unless we hand
over the suspect immediately.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:50.090
All right, I'll have a word with them.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.360
Miharu...

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.900
Commander!

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:56.070
Commander, please have a
helicopter readied at once!

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:56.830
Commander! Message from the tower!
Commander, please have a
helicopter readied at once!

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.300
Commander! Message from the tower!

00:15:58.300 --> 00:15:59.840
A large transport vehicle is rushing
towards Gate 12.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.830
It looks as if they're not going
wait to be let inside!

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:04.010
Shit!

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:13.450
SSDF vehicle is inside the complex.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.790
They've stopped ten meters from
the end of the runway One.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:14.950
Launch our Scramble ready
flight squadron!
They've stopped ten meters from
the end of the runway One.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.050
Launch our Scramble ready
flight squadron!

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:18.190
Launch our fighters?

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:18.560
Yes, the only arms we have here are
anti-air missiles and AA guns.
Launch our fighters?

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:22.130
Yes, the only arms we have here are
anti-air missiles and AA guns.

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:24.260
We'll have the fighters deal
with the intruders.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.100
Yes, Sir.

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.000
Remaining here puts you in danger.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.590
I'll get you your airlift, but for now
we must get you to safety.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:32.340
Is she there?

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:32.970
Dead ahead, distance 3000.
Is she there?

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.340
Dead ahead, distance 3000.

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.710
Where that transport aircraft is.
Get ready.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:40.240
No, let me take it from here.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:42.250
That's too dangerous!

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.080
But this is my own personal mission.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:46.550
But still...

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:51.460
All right. Go, Yushiro.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:53.190
Are you insane, Captain Ataka!

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:56.090
Kaburagi, Yushiro is a pilot.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.770
Yushiro, I'll begin the countdown
five seconds before launch.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:03.230
Roger.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:10.510
Five, four, three, two, one...

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:11.980
Go!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.150
Yushiro, we don't have a C&C vehicle,

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:26.260
but I'll use my unit to give you as
much backup as I can provide.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:28.090
Roger.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.560
Good luck...

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:46.180
Raptor!

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.450
Captain Gowa! Three more F-22's
are coming your way!

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.920
Ground them before they take off!

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:02.830
What's the situation?!

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:03.230
The intruder is moving at sixty klicks.
What's the situation?!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.660
The intruder is moving at sixty klicks.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.430
It's probably a wheeled
armored vehicle.

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:08.170
Contact the F-22's!

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:10.230
I want it destroyed as soon as
they have it in their sights.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.270
Destroyed? But Sir, what about
the Japanese SSDF?

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:15.600
That's my direct order! I'll
take full responsibility.

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:19.330
I won't let intruders trespass on this
base without paying a price.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.550
Captain Gowa, watch your back!

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:51.960
Yushiro, increase the range of your
infrared detector to maximum!

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:55.750
I'll send you the ballpark data.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:58.150
Combine it with your data and that
should tell you where they are.

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:01.480
I can't keep up with it!

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:14.860
Yushiro, abort operations!
Get out of there!

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.560
Your chances against them
are next to nil! Yushiro!

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:26.640
What's wrong, Miharu?

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.560
How can it evade fire like that?

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:40.790
Is the intruder really an
armored vehicle?

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:44.060
Could it be...
The SSDF's bipedal weapon?

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:51.200
FV201, this is Hull. Change
your pattern of fire.

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.170
Switch to wide dispersal fire pattern.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.230
I want you to spray bullets all
around that intruder.

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.970
FV201, roger.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.990
Yushiro, get out of there! Yushiro!

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:14.120
A TA's no match against an airborne
fighter! Do you want to die?!

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:19.990
That blockhead!

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:23.690
Ataka, hurry!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:04.840
Impact!

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:13.920
CB3 has detected GS emissions
coming out of Japan.

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:16.690
From the Gowa's old home?
Somewhere else?

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.990
Sir, it's coming from some
place in Tokyo.

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.620
Within Tokyo?

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:22.090
Not Yokota?

00:21:26.730 --> 00:21:28.200
The Threshold...

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:31.770
Up!

00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:33.750
Hark

00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:40.300
It's time I journey

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:50.970
Break apart my heart

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:57.500
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.830 --> 00:23:05.010
Pours out from it

00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:08.930
I can only, oh

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:12.120
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:17.730
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:36.830
I can only, oh

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:39.980
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:45.180
I pray, let this break apart

00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:02.950
The absolute nothingness...

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:05.260
The oppressive passions...

00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:08.360
All coalesce into a raging current that
hungers to consume everything.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:11.520
Its intensity... its sadness...

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:15.700
Could, in a heartbeat, doom this world
to become a puff of smoke.

00:24:16.670 --> 00:24:18.440
We face each other

00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:21.210
Projecting our thoughts and hopes,
hearts captivated

00:24:21.210 --> 00:24:24.440
They become the personifications
of sentiment

00:24:25.340 --> 00:24:27.540
Thirst dominates the hearts of all.
